.\" The linuxio(8) man page, written by hand. Every statement in it is held
.\" to the code of the CLI (backend/cli) and the units in packaging/systemd.
.TH LINUXIO 8 "" "LinuxIO" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
linuxio \- manage the LinuxIO services
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxio
.B status
.br
.B linuxio
.B logs
.RI [ component ]
.RI [ lines ]
.br
.B linuxio
.B start
.br
.B linuxio
.B stop
.br
.B linuxio
.B restart
.RB [ \-\-full ]
.br
.B linuxio
.B verbose
.BR enable | disable | status
.br
.B linuxio
.B version
.br
.B linuxio
.B help
.SH DESCRIPTION
LinuxIO is a web interface for administering a Linux server.
It listens on TCP port 8090
.RB ( linuxio\-webserver.socket )
and signs users in through PAM.
.PP
.B linuxio
is the only LinuxIO program meant to be typed.
It shows the state and the logs of the LinuxIO systemd units, starts,
stops and restarts them, and turns debug logging on and off.
The other LinuxIO programs live in
.I /usr/libexec/linuxio
and are started by systemd and by LinuxIO itself, not by hand.
.PP
Run without a command,
.B linuxio
prints the list of commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
List every loaded systemd unit whose name begins with
.BR linuxio ,
with its load, active and sub state and its description.
Needs no root.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \fIcomponent\fR "] [" \fIlines\fR ]
Print the last
.I lines
entries of the LinuxIO journal (100 when not given) and follow the journal
until interrupted.
.I component
is one of
.B webserver
(also
.B web
or
.BR server ),
.BR bridge ,
.BR auth ,
.B indexer
(also
.BR index )
and
.B monitoring
(also
.BR monitor );
without one, the entries of those five and of
.B linuxio\-worker
are shown, with those of every unit listed under
.BR "SYSTEMD UNITS" .
Needs root or membership of the
.B systemd\-journal
or
.B adm
group.
A user added to one of those groups after signing in is served through
.BR sg (1).
.TP
.B start
Start
.BR linuxio.target .
Needs root.
.TP
.B stop
Stop
.B linuxio.target
and the units that are part of it.
The job hosts
.RB ( linuxio\-jobs@ \fIuid\fR .service )
and the btrfs units outside the target keep running.
Needs root.
.TP
.BR restart " [" \-\-full ]
Without
.BR \-\-full ,
restart
.BR linuxio\-bridge\-socket\-user.service ,
.B linuxio\-auth.socket
and
.BR linuxio\-webserver.service ,
leaving
.B linuxio\-webserver.socket
listening on its port.
With
.BR \-\-full ,
restart
.B linuxio.target
and wait for
.B linuxio\-webserver.socket
to listen again, starting it again up to three times while it cannot listen, as when
another process still holds the port for a moment.
Needs root.
.TP
.BR verbose " " enable | disable | status
.B enable
writes a drop-in that adds
.B \-\-verbose
to the command line of
.BR linuxio\-webserver.service ,
.B linuxio\-indexer.service
and
.BR linuxio\-monitoring.service ,
reloads systemd and has each running daemon reload, so that it logs at debug
level.
Sessions already signed in switch at their next sign-in.
.B disable
removes the drop-ins and reloads the same way.
.B status
says whether verbose mode is enabled and lists the drop-ins.
.B enable
and
.B disable
need root;
.B status
does not.
The same switch is in the Settings page of the web interface.
.TP
.B version
Print the version of LinuxIO, which is that of the installed package.
.B linuxio \-\-version
prints the same.
Needs no root.
.TP
.B help
Print the list of commands; so do
.BR \-h ,
.B \-\-help
and no command at all.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B linuxio
exits 0 on success, 1 when a command fails, and 2 for a command it does not
know.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/linuxio
This command.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/linuxio/
The other LinuxIO programs.
.TP
.I /etc/linuxio/
Configuration:
.I disallowed\-users
(the users PAM refuses to sign in, root by default),
.I indexer/config.yaml
and
.IR monitoring/config.yaml ,
and the settings saved from the web interface.
.TP
.I /var/lib/linuxio/
State: the web server's TLS certificate under
.IR webserver/ ,
the job records under
.IR jobs/ ,
the file index under
.I indexer/
and the metrics history under
.IR monitoring/ .
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/linuxio
The PAM stack of the sign-in.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/linuxio*
The units listed below.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/linuxio\-webserver.service.d/verbose.conf
.TQ
.I /etc/systemd/system/linuxio\-indexer.service.d/verbose.conf
.TQ
.I /etc/systemd/system/linuxio\-monitoring.service.d/verbose.conf
The drop-ins of
.BR "linuxio verbose enable" .
.SH SYSTEMD UNITS
.B linuxio.target
groups the units LinuxIO runs; it is enabled at install and wanted by
.BR multi\-user.target .
Part of it:
.TP
.BR linuxio\-webserver.socket ", " linuxio\-webserver.service
The web server, started by the first connection to port 8090.
.TP
.BR linuxio\-auth.socket ", " linuxio\-auth@.service
The sign-in helper, one instance per connection from the web server on
.IR /run/linuxio/auth.sock .
.TP
.B linuxio\-bridge\-socket\-user.service
Creates the group that lets the web server connect to the sign-in socket.
.TP
.BR linuxio\-indexer.socket ", " linuxio\-indexer.service
The file indexer, started on demand and stopped when idle.
.TP
.BR linuxio\-indexer\-index.timer ", " linuxio\-indexer\-index.service
The periodic full index.
.TP
.B linuxio\-monitoring.service
The metrics collector.
.TP
.B linuxio\-issue.service
Writes the addresses LinuxIO answers on into the login banner.
.TP
.BR linuxio\-btrfs\-health.timer ", " linuxio\-btrfs\-health.service
The periodic btrfs pool check, enabled on hosts with btrfs.
.PP
Outside the target, so that stopping or restarting LinuxIO leaves them
running:
.TP
.BR linuxio\-jobs@ \fIuid\fR .socket ", " linuxio\-jobs@ \fIuid\fR .service
The job host of one user, which runs the jobs that user starts from the
web interface.
.TP
.B linuxio\-btrfs\-degraded.service
At boot, mounts degraded the btrfs pools in
.I /etc/fstab
that miss a disk; enabled on hosts with btrfs.
.TP
.BR linuxio\-btrfs\-resync@ \fIuuid\fR .service ", " linuxio\-btrfs\-rebuild@ \fIuuid\fR .service
Repair a btrfs pool, started by the pool check.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the state of the LinuxIO units:
.PP
.RS
.nf
linuxio status
.fi
.RE
.PP
Follow the bridge's log, starting from its last 200 entries:
.PP
.RS
.nf
linuxio logs bridge 200
.fi
.RE
.PP
Restart the web server and the sign-in without closing port 8090, then
everything:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo linuxio restart
sudo linuxio restart \-\-full
.fi
.RE
.PP
Log at debug level, then stop:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo linuxio verbose enable
sudo linuxio verbose disable
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR sg (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5),
.BR pam (8)
